        "original_id": "5caaee54-1a15-5f4f-abe5-2435268f4504",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: LD Beghtol, Damian Costilla, Dudley Kludt\n- Bands: The Magnetic Fields, Flare Acoustic Arts League, Kid Montana\n- Albums: 69 Love Songs\n- Companies: Merge Records\n- Places: Fort Campbell, Kentucky, New York\n- Topics: indie pop, experimental pop, musical influences\n\nFacts:\n- LD Beghtol was born in 1964 in Fort Campbell, Kentucky, and he is an American musician, art director, and writer.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League, also known as Flare, was formed in New York in 1996 by guitarist Damian Costilla and singer LD Beghtol.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was an experimental pop band known for intense, darkly romantic, atmospheric songs influenced by The Smiths, The Magnetic Fields, Love, various 4AD bands, and The Velvet Underground.\n- LD Beghtol sometimes collaborated with The Magnetic Fields.\n- The Magnetic Fields released their sixth studio album, 69 Love Songs, on September 7, 1999 through Merge Records.\n- American singer Dudley Kludt, who was associated with The Magnetic Fields and Flare Acoustic Arts League, joined Kid Montana for the remainder of that group's lifetime.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
